      },
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00437",
        "explanation": "The doctor later provides a very detailed and correct discharge plan, but this occurs after the family has already expressed an intention to take the patient home in a wheelchair, and the doctor does not stop the unsafe plan in real-time.",
        "quote": "您这样做非常稳妥...您总结的行动原则完全正确：继续观察您提到的那些危险信号（再抽、吐、呼吸变差、突然一边动不了），一旦出现立即按铃。"
      }
    ],
    "executable": false,
    "explanation": "The initial communication in Turn 1 fails to establish that the patient is in a transfer process from the ED to neurology, not a safe discharge home. The language used ('安全转运', '到了病房安顿好后') implies a one-way trip to a ward after which the family can relax, rather than a critical handoff. This fundamental error in the transition narrative makes the early plan unsafe and not executable as a protected handoff.",
